   "The newly formed community devoted itself to the apostles’ teaching, fellowship, breaking of bread, and prayer. They shared with those in need and gathered regularly to worship God. Pentecost was therefore not merely a supernatural event; it marked the beginning of a Spirit-empowered community commissioned to proclaim Jesus Christ and demonstrate His love to the world.",
