     "The meeting had been important, but it was not the end of his service.",
     "The narrative presents Philip as someone who continued proclaiming the gospel in other places.",
     "This reinforces a central lesson from the entire story: faithful discipleship is not limited to a single conversation, event, or achievement.",
     "There will be moments when we help someone take an important step. There will also be moments when we must continue serving others in different settings.",
     "Philip remained engaged in the mission.",
     "Trusting God With the Next Stage",
     "Philip and the official did not continue travelling together.",
     "The official returned toward his home, while Philip continued preaching in other towns.",
     "The account does not tell us exactly how the official’s spiritual life developed after the encounter, so we should not claim details that are not recorded.",
     "Nevertheless, the separation offers a useful lesson about discipleship.",
     "A person who teaches or mentors another believer does not need to control that person’s entire future.",
     "The responsibility is to serve faithfully, communicate the truth, and help the other person grow toward a mature relationship with Jesus.",
     "Christian discipleship includes walking alongside people, but it also involves recognising that each person must continue responding to God in their own life.",
     "Philip’s role in the official’s journey was significant, even though their time together was brief.",
     "A Story That Continues Beyond the Road",
     "The encounter began with a direction to travel toward Gaza.",
     "It developed into a conversation about Scripture, a proclamation of Jesus, and a baptism.",
     "It concluded with the official rejoicing and Philip continuing his ministry elsewhere.",
     "The road became a place where the gospel crossed geographical and cultural boundaries.",
     "The story reminds us that God’s mission can advance through ordinary acts of obedience, thoughtful explanation, and personal encounters.",
     "One person travelled with questions. Another person was willing to help.",
     "Through that encounter, the official heard the good news about Jesus and continued his journey rejoicing."
