   "Memory Verse",
   "Acts 20:24 (KJV)",
   "“But none of these things move me, neither count I my life dear unto myself, so that I might finish my course with joy, and the ministry, which I have received of the Lord Jesus, to testify the gospel of the grace of God.”",
   "Memory Verse Reflection",
   "Paul’s words reveal a life directed by a clear purpose. He knew that following Christ would involve suffering, uncertainty, and opposition, but he remained determined to complete the ministry entrusted to him.",
   "His example challenges believers to consider what truly directs their lives. It is possible to begin a responsibility with enthusiasm but lose commitment when difficulties arise. Paul reminds us that faithfulness requires perseverance.",
   "The goal is not simply to start well, gain recognition, or avoid hardship. It is to remain obedient to Christ and complete the work He has given us.",
