     "This was a different setting from the synagogue gatherings described in several other accounts of Paul’s missionary work. The narrative does not mention a synagogue in Philippi. Instead, it tells us about a riverside gathering where women had come together for prayer.",
     "Paul and his companions recognised the opportunity to share the message of God with the people present.",
