     "Nevertheless, they continued to direct their attention toward God.",
     "The story does not require us to imagine that Paul and Silas felt no pain or struggled with no emotions. Prayer and praise are not evidence that a person is incapable of distress. Rather, their actions demonstrate that suffering did not have to determine the direction of their faith.",
