     "The commander arrested Paul and ordered him to be bound with two chains. He then attempted to determine who Paul was and what he had done.",
     "But the crowd was in confusion. Some shouted one thing, while others shouted something different. The commander could not establish the truth because the people were giving conflicting explanations.",
     "The violence became so severe that the soldiers had to carry Paul away to protect him from the mob. The crowd followed, shouting for his death.",
     "The scene was a striking contrast. Paul had come to Jerusalem to worship and participate in the life of his people, but he was now being carried away by Roman soldiers while an angry crowd demanded his destruction.",
     "The Roman intervention did not mean that the authorities fully understood Paul’s innocence or the nature of his mission. At this stage, the commander was attempting to restore order and discover what had happened.",
     "Yet the intervention created an opportunity for Paul to speak.",
