     "A violent wind, known as a northeaster, swept down from the island. The storm struck the vessel with such force that the sailors could no longer maintain their intended course.",
     "The ship was caught and carried along by the wind.",
     "The crew struggled to control the vessel. They sailed under the shelter of a small island called Clauda and managed to secure the ship’s boat, which was being dragged behind them. They then used ropes or cables to undergird the ship, strengthening the structure in an effort to prevent it from breaking apart.",
