     "These islanders did not know Paul as a prominent apostle or a man who had stood before governors and kings. They saw a group of exhausted strangers who needed warmth, shelter, and assistance.",
     "Their hospitality became an important part of the story.",
     "Paul joined the others in gathering sticks for the fire. As he placed a bundle of sticks on the flames, a viper came out because of the heat and fastened itself to his hand.",
