     "He also allowed the visitors into the place where he was staying, showing a willingness to engage with people connected to a Gentile household.",
     "Peter’s understanding was developing through a sequence of events. God did not necessarily explain everything to him at once. Instead, the vision, the arrival of the messengers, and the Holy Spirit’s instruction worked together to prepare him for what was coming.",
     "We sometimes expect God to explain every detail before we act. Yet Peter’s experience teaches us the importance of responding faithfully to the direction we have received while remaining attentive to how God continues to clarify the situation.",
     "The meeting between Peter and Cornelius would not have happened if Peter had ignored the messengers or refused to leave Joppa.",
     "The gospel’s advance required both divine preparation and human obedience."
