    "assignment": {
     "title": null,
     "text": "Answer the following questions in your own words, using Scripture to support your answers.\n1. Who was Cornelius, and what characteristics of his life are described in Acts 10:1–2?\n2. What instruction did Cornelius receive through the angel’s appearance?\n3. What did Peter see in his vision, and what command did he receive?\n4. Why did Peter initially resist the command to eat the animals in the vision?\n5. How did the arrival of Cornelius’s messengers help Peter understand that God was directing him?\n6. What did Peter learn about treating people from other nations?\n7. Why had Cornelius gathered his relatives and close friends?\n8. What were the central elements of Peter’s message about Jesus in Acts 10:34–43?\n9. What happened while Peter was speaking to Cornelius’s household?\n10. Why were the Jewish believers astonished when the Holy Spirit came upon the Gentiles?\n11. Why did Peter ask whether anyone could forbid water baptism to these believers?\n12. What concern did some believers in Jerusalem raise when Peter returned?\n13. How did Peter explain and defend his decision to visit Cornelius?\n14. What was the response of the Jerusalem believers after hearing Peter’s explanation?\n15. What does this story teach us about the relationship between evangelism and discipleship?\n16. How can cultural prejudice prevent believers from recognizing God’s work?\n17. What is the difference between maintaining biblical convictions and rejecting people because of their background?\n18. How can the principles of this story be applied in churches, schools, workplaces, and international communities?\n19. Why should the gospel remain centred on the person and work of Jesus Christ?\n20. What is one change you can make in your own attitudes or behaviour in response to this topic?\n\nAssignment\nImagine that members of a Christian community are concerned because people from a different cultural background have begun attending their gatherings.\nWrite a response that applies the lessons of Acts 11:1–18.\nYour response should explain:\n• Why believers should examine their assumptions.\n• Why Scripture must guide the Church’s decisions.\n• How leaders can respond patiently to concerns.\n• Why people should not be excluded from Christian fellowship merely because they are culturally different.\n• How the community can support new believers in growing in Christ.\nWHOLE-TOPIC DISCUSSION — GOD WELCOMES PEOPLE FROM EVERY NATION"
    }
