     "Faith that exists only in speech, without influencing the way a person lives, fails to demonstrate the kind of trust in God that transforms behaviour.",
     "James then made a statement that has often been misunderstood when separated from the wider teaching of Scripture: faith without works is dead.",
     "He was not teaching that people can purchase salvation through charitable actions or earn forgiveness by accumulating good deeds.",
     "Rather, he was challenging the claim that a person possesses genuine faith when their life consistently displays no evidence of that faith.",
     "Paul and James addressed different aspects of the relationship between faith and works.",
     "Paul emphasized that people are justified by God’s grace through faith, not by works that give them grounds for boasting. James confronted people who claimed to have faith while refusing to demonstrate its reality through their conduct.",
     "Ephesians 2:8–10 holds these truths together. Salvation is by grace through faith, not the result of works; yet believers are created in Christ Jesus for good works that God prepared for them to walk in.",
     "Good works are not the price paid for salvation. They are a fitting expression of a life being transformed by God’s grace.",
     "James illustrated his argument through Abraham.",
