     "He also confronted the danger of friendship with the world when that phrase describes allegiance to values that oppose God. His concern was not that Christians should avoid every relationship with people outside the Church. Rather, he warned against allowing pride, envy, selfishness, and disloyalty to shape the believer’s life.",
