     "Biblical knowledge should produce practical obedience. James consistently challenged believers to live according to the truth they professed.",
     "Wise leadership requires both conviction and humility. James considered testimony, Scripture, and the needs of the community. Christian leaders should combine biblical faithfulness with careful judgment.",
     "The treatment of vulnerable people reveals the character of a community. James emphasized care for those in need and condemned favouritism. The Church should demonstrate the compassion of Christ.",
     "Every believer contributes to the mission of discipleship. Not everyone will hold a formal leadership position, but everyone can grow in character, encourage others, and put God’s Word into practice."
