     "Their response was immediate. They left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired servants and followed Jesus.",
     "The passage does not tell us every thought that passed through John’s mind at that moment. It does, however, show that the call of Jesus required a decisive response.",
     "John was being invited into a different kind of life.",
     "Instead of concentrating exclusively on the work he had previously known, he would become a disciple of a teacher whose ministry would lead him through villages, towns, synagogues, and gatherings of people who needed to hear the kingdom of God proclaimed.",
     "Following Jesus would involve learning, travelling, serving, and witnessing events that John could not yet fully understand.",
     "John did not know everything that lay ahead. He had not yet witnessed the crucifixion or the resurrection. He did not yet understand the full significance of Jesus’s identity and mission.",
     "Nevertheless, he began following the One who had called him.",
     "This beginning teaches us something important about discipleship. Following Jesus is not simply agreeing with certain teachings. It involves allowing Him to reshape our priorities, our understanding, our relationships, and the direction of our lives.",
