     "The Gospel concludes its statement of purpose by explaining that the recorded signs were written so that readers might believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God, and that believing they might have life through His name.",
     "This purpose is central to understanding John’s work as a witness.",
     "His Gospel is not merely a collection of memories about Jesus. It is a carefully arranged testimony intended to reveal Christ and call readers to faith.",
     "John also records that Jesus is the good shepherd who lays down His life for the sheep. He presents Jesus as the One who reveals the Father and promises eternal life to those who believe in Him.",
