     "The passage presents John as a witness who shared in the suffering associated with his commitment to Christ.",
     "He was not writing from a position of comfort and worldly influence. He was describing his experience as a servant of Jesus who remained connected to the Church despite his circumstances.",
     "On the Lord’s day, John says that he was in the Spirit and heard a loud voice behind him, like a trumpet.",
     "The voice instructed him to write what he saw in a book and send it to the seven churches in Asia.",
     "When John turned to see the voice, he saw seven golden lampstands and, among them, one like the Son of man.",
     "The description of the figure was filled with imagery drawn from the language of Scripture. His clothing, appearance, and voice communicated majesty and authority.",
