     "title": null,
     "text": "Answer the following questions in your own words, supporting your answers with Scripture.\n1. What was John’s occupation before he became a disciple of Jesus?\n2. What does Mark 1:19–20 reveal about John’s response to the call of Jesus?\n3. What does the name “Sons of Thunder” suggest when considered alongside Luke 9:51–56?\n4. How did Jesus correct James and John’s understanding of greatness in Mark 10:35–45?\n5. What did Jesus teach His disciples about love and service during the events recorded in John 13?\n6. What responsibility did Jesus entrust to the beloved disciple at the cross?\n7. What did John and Peter discover when they went to the tomb?\n8. Why is the resurrection essential to John’s witness and the Christian gospel?\n9. What happened when Peter and John encountered the man at the temple gate?\n10. Why were Peter and John brought before the religious authorities in Acts 4?\n11. How did the apostles respond when they were ordered to stop teaching in the name of Jesus?\n12. What purpose does John identify for writing his Gospel in John 20:30–31?\n13. What does John’s First Epistle teach about walking in the light?\n14. Why does John emphasize that love must be expressed through actions?\n15. What does it mean to test the spirits according to 1 John 4:1–6?\n16. How can believers evaluate spiritual teaching without becoming unnecessarily suspicious or arrogant?\n17. What circumstances does John describe in Revelation 1:9–20?\n18. How does the vision of the risen Christ encourage believers who face suffering?\n19. What can contemporary Christian communities learn from the messages to the seven churches in Revelation?\n20. What practical changes can you make to become a more faithful witness to Jesus Christ?\n\nAssignment\nRead Revelation 1:9–20.\nWrite a reflection on John’s description of Jesus as the Living One who was dead and is alive forevermore.\nThen read one of the messages to the seven churches in Revelation 2–3.\nIdentify:\n• What the church was commended for.\n• What problem or weakness was addressed.\n• What response Jesus called for.\n• What lesson contemporary believers can learn.\nConclude by writing a prayer asking God to help you remain faithful to Jesus Christ in both favourable and difficult circumstances.\nWHOLE-TOPIC DISCUSSION — JOHN’S WITNESS TO JESUS AND HIS CHURCH"
