     "Barnabas could have continued working alone and attempted to manage every responsibility. Instead, he recognized Saul’s abilities and brought him into the work.",
     "The decision reflected humility and wisdom.",
     "Barnabas was not threatened by the possibility that another gifted teacher might receive attention. He understood that the needs of the growing church were more important than protecting his own position.",
     "Saul possessed a strong knowledge of Scripture and a calling to proclaim Jesus among the Gentiles. Barnabas recognized that these abilities could help the believers in Antioch mature.",
     "The two men worked together, teaching the community and strengthening its understanding of the faith.",
