     "One example Paul named was the teaching of Hymenaeus and Philetus, who had strayed from the truth by claiming that the resurrection had already taken place. Their teaching was upsetting the faith of some believers.",
     "Timothy needed to resist such errors by remaining grounded in the truth.",
     "Paul’s instruction was not simply to speak confidently. He called Timothy to become a worker who correctly handled God’s Word. That required careful study, sound understanding, and the humility to submit personal opinions to Scripture.",
     "The responsibility applies to everyone who teaches the Bible, whether in a church, a discipleship gathering, a family, or a personal conversation.",
     "A passage must be understood in its context. A person’s preferred opinion must not be presented as though it were explicitly stated in Scripture. Difficult questions should be approached honestly rather than answered with invented details.",
