     "Timothy’s ministry required more than a promising beginning. Paul wanted him to remain faithful throughout his life.",
     "In 1 Timothy, Paul addressed him as a man of God and urged him to flee destructive desires and pursue righteousness, godliness, faith, love, endurance, and gentleness.",
     "He instructed Timothy to fight the good fight of faith and take hold of eternal life. Timothy had been called to follow Christ and had made a public confession of his faith.",
     "Paul placed this calling within the larger reality of God’s authority and Christ’s appearing. Timothy’s service was not simply a personal project. It was a responsibility carried before God.",
