     "title": "Comprehensive Check — Timothy: A Young Leader Raised to Serve the Church",
     "text": "Answer the following questions in your own words. Use the Scriptures from this topic to support your answers.\nSECTION A — UNDERSTANDING TIMOTHY’S STORY\n1. Who were Lois and Eunice, and how did they influence Timothy’s faith?\n2. In which cities did believers speak well of Timothy?\n3. Why did Paul invite Timothy to accompany him?\n4. What responsibility did Timothy receive when Paul sent him to encourage the Thessalonian believers?\n5. How did Paul describe Timothy’s concern for the believers in Philippi?\nSECTION B — CHARACTER AND LEADERSHIP\n1. According to 1 Timothy 4:12, in which five areas was Timothy to become an example to believers?\n2. Why did Paul emphasize both Timothy’s life and his teaching?\n3. What does the command to train oneself for godliness teach about spiritual growth?\n4. What does Paul’s instruction to fan into flame the gift of God suggest about developing one’s abilities?\n5. Why should Christian leaders remain willing to receive correction?\nSECTION C — TRUTH AND DISCIPLESHIP\n1. Why did Paul warn Timothy about false teaching and destructive arguments?\n2. What does it mean to handle the word of truth correctly?\n3. According to 2 Timothy 3:16–17, what purposes does Scripture serve?\n4. Why did Paul instruct Timothy to preach the Word with patience and careful teaching?\n5. What qualities should characterize a person entrusted with teaching others?\nSECTION D — PERSEVERANCE AND MULTIPLICATION\n1. Explain Paul’s illustrations of the soldier, athlete, and farmer.\n2. How can believers remain faithful when their service becomes difficult?\n3. Explain the pattern of discipleship described in 2 Timothy 2:2.\n4. Why should discipleship aim to equip people to help others grow?\n5. What does Timothy’s story teach you about remaining faithful to Christ throughout life?\nSECTION E — PERSONAL APPLICATION\n1. Which person has helped shape your faith, and what have you learned from that person?\n2. In what area of character do you most need to become a better example?\n3. What can you do to improve your understanding of Scripture?\n4. Who could you encourage or help grow spiritually during the coming month?\n5. What is one practical commitment you will make after studying Timothy’s life?"
