     "The man who had entered Damascus in pursuit of believers had become a recipient of their ministry. He had depended on others during his blindness, and now he began to live among the disciples.",
     "The transformation was remarkable, but it was not the end of Saul’s journey. He would still need to learn, grow, face opposition, and demonstrate through his life that his change was genuine.",
     "His past would not disappear from history. The persecution he had carried out remained part of his story. But it would no longer determine the direction of his obedience to Christ.",
